From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SQ2 Mesa fork
Subject: [PATCH] d3d12: experimental SQ2 force-on for shader images

Experiment only, behind D3D12_SQ2_FORCE_IMAGES=1. Overrides each
failing check inside can_shader_image_load_all_formats AFTER the probe
patch has printed the real values, so a forced run still records the
true TypedUAV flag and per-format table on stderr. Requires the probe
patch applied first (CI applies probe for inputs probe|force|both).

With the variable unset this patch changes nothing: real checks run,
real result returned. With it set, each ignored failure is logged.

Forces support_shader_images=true so ARB_shader_image_load_store and
(via st_extensions.c) ARB_compute_shader can expose on drivers whose
TypedUAV/format queries fail (e.g. Qualcomm 27.x). No lowering is
added by this patch: any shader that actually loads an image format
the hardware rejects will fail at pipeline creation or render
wrong pixels -- that failure list defines the real lowering work
(see d3d12_lower_image_casts.c, already in-tree). Keep EEVEE fenced
in Blender while this is set: EEVEE reads SFLOAT_16_16_16_16 and
wider formats that have no R32 lowering.

Unset the variable for comparison runs.

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_screen.cpp b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_screen.cpp
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_screen.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_screen.cpp
@@ -921,9 +921,13 @@ can_shader_image_load_all_formats(struct d3d12_screen *screen)
    fprintf(stderr, "D3D12 SQ2: TypedUAVLoadAdditionalFormats=%d\n",
            (int)screen->opts.TypedUAVLoadAdditionalFormats);
    if (!screen->opts.TypedUAVLoadAdditionalFormats)
-      return false;
+   {
+      if (!os_get_option("D3D12_SQ2_FORCE_IMAGES"))
+         return false;
+      fprintf(stderr, "D3D12 SQ2: TypedUAV flag false, forcing past it (experimental)\n");
+   }

@@ -949,8 +953,12 @@ can_shader_image_load_all_formats(struct d3d12_screen *screen)
       fprintf(stderr, "D3D12 SQ2: fmt %d hr=0x%lx tuav=%d load=%d store=%d\n",
               (int)additional_formats[i], (long)hr, tuav, load, store);
-      if (!tuav || !load || !store)
-         return false;
+      if (!tuav || !load || !store) {
+         if (!os_get_option("D3D12_SQ2_FORCE_IMAGES"))
+            return false;
+         fprintf(stderr, "D3D12 SQ2: forcing past failed format (experimental)\n");
+      }
    }

    return true;
